@flexiarg problems/pattern-genesis-from-evidence-bearing-holes
@title Problem node: no existing pattern expresses a recurring way of acting (catalogue R17-triple-prime)
@keywords problem-node, R17mint, pattern-genesis, vocabulary-enlargement, policy-holes, catalogue
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why catalogue authority: p4ng/sec-catalog.tex paragraph R17-triple-prime (pat:r17mint), IF/HOWEVER quoted verbatim with file:line; distinct from the dossier R17 node problems/r17-structure-learning, whose problem is model reduction -- this node is the catalogue's minting problem, enlarging the vocabulary, and deliberately carries no @holds-at so it cannot be confused with structure learning
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; the catalogue's THEN names the mechanism (bundle circumstances, memories, near-matches and a falsifiable outcome into a candidate pattern, minted at an unearned prior, promoted only by witnessed outcomes and review)

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node from the catalogue's R17-triple-prime paragraph: retrieval, composition, embedding nearness and structure learning can only work with the patterns that already exist, so a recurring way of acting with no adequate pattern needs a minting path.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L16 from the sec-catalog pattern paragraphs. Duplicate check: the existing problems/r17-structure-learning quotes the dossier's model-reduction problem; no existing node states the vocabulary-enlargement problem, so this node is not a duplicate.

  + IF:
    Repeated, independently recorded episodes, failed retrievals, or fold policy-holes show that no existing pattern adequately expresses a recurring way of acting.

  + HOWEVER:
    The catalogue's tension, verbatim: "If repeated, independently recorded episodes, failed retrievals, or fold policy-holes show that no existing pattern adequately expresses a recurring way of acting. \textbf{However} R6 can retrieve only the patterns already written down, R13 can compose only the moves already in the vocabulary, embedding nearness proposes similarity rather than a new action, and structure learning can reduce or compare the structures it has but cannot author a missing one." (source: p4ng sec-catalog.tex:346, paragraph "Pattern Genesis from Evidence-Bearing Holes (R17''')", label pat:r17mint)

  + THEN:
    This node is the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer pattern genesis; the minting mechanism is the catalogue's THEN, not this node's to restate.

  + BECAUSE:
    Structure learning must sometimes enlarge the vocabulary in which policies can be expressed, not only rearrange or simplify an inherited vocabulary (the catalogue's Because clause, same paragraph, citing smith2020structure).

    + evidence: p4ng sec-catalog.tex:346 (pat:r17mint paragraph, If/However/Then/Because); duplicate-check receipt runs/L16-duplicate-check.edn.
